          "Verification for temporary assignment letters means checking the destination record, not the activity log. A sent message or a closed task proves that someone acted, but it does not prove that the employee record or the access state changed. Confirm the field or outcome the work was supposed to affect. If the destination cannot be checked, the case is not complete. At HR Coordinators, the temporary assignment letters close note names the record that was inspected.",
          "A close note should say what was checked, who approved it, what changed, and what would reopen the case. The HR owner should be able to read one record later and understand why it closed without contacting the original coordinator. At HR Coordinators, the temporary assignment letters close note is kept with the source evidence. The note should not restate the whole history."
